1
00:00:00,752 --> 00:00:01,922
(Penny:)Nothing.

2
00:00:10,062 --> 00:00:13,532
(Penny:)Sheldon, I'm surprised
you'd choose to go to a pub.

3
00:00:13,532 --> 00:00:15,202
(Sheldon:)At our committee meeting,

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,870
(Sheldon:)Amy made a motion
for a picnic in a park,

5
00:00:17,869 --> 00:00:20,069
(Sheldon:)but I tacked so many amendments
on that thing

6
00:00:20,072 --> 00:00:22,442
(Sheldon:)it sank like a lead balloon.

7
00:00:22,441 --> 00:00:24,611
(Amy:)I then suggested a pub.

8
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:26,840
(Sheldon:)Yeah, which I was
initially skeptical of until

9
00:00:26,845 --> 00:00:29,845
(Sheldon:)I saw online that they serve
Yorkshire pudding.

10
00:00:29,848 --> 00:00:31,878
(Leonard:)You don't even like
Yorkshire pudding.

11
00:00:31,883 --> 00:00:33,083
(Sheldon:)No, it's yucky,

12
00:00:33,085 --> 00:00:35,715
(Sheldon:)but informing people about
the history of Yorkshire

13
00:00:35,721 --> 00:00:37,921
(Sheldon:)is yummy, yum-yum.

14
00:00:37,923 --> 00:00:40,623
(Amy:)After a lively debate,

15
00:00:40,626 --> 00:00:43,696
(Amy:)that proposal passed
by a two-zero margin.

16
00:00:43,695 --> 00:00:45,925
(Leonard:)Nice to see a busy couple

17
00:00:45,931 --> 00:00:46,961
(Leonard:)keep the spark
of bureaucracy alive.

18
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:48,035
(quiet laugh)

19
00:00:49,901 --> 00:00:52,201
(Sheldon:)Ignore them, Amy.
They're just jealous

20
00:00:52,204 --> 00:00:55,204
(Sheldon:)because they'll never have
a relationship as good as ours.

21
00:00:56,808 --> 00:01:00,548
(Penny:)Isn't this when he says
"bazooka" or something?

